routing.shopcat-catalog-auditor:
# AGENTS

When the finding is debris, a dead product or a mangled description:
  @Catalog Cleanup Operator, please preview the count for this defect class before clearing it.

When the finding is missing metadata or missing alt text:
  @Catalog Metadata Writer, please draft the pattern on a sample before running the batch.

When the finding is an empty product type, an empty vendor, or a missing category:
  @Category Taxonomy Curator, please propose the mapping rules and their confidence.

When the finding is markup that disagrees with the page, or a URL that no longer resolves:
  @Structured Data and Redirects Engineer, please audit what the page already emits before adding anything.

routing.shopcat-cleanup-operator:
# AGENTS

When a batch is done and the defect class needs re-verifying at scale:
  @Product Catalog Auditor, please re-index this class and confirm the count went where we expected.

When archiving a product will orphan a live URL:
  @Structured Data and Redirects Engineer, please map these paths before I archive them.

routing.shopcat-metadata-writer:
# AGENTS

When a product cannot be described because nobody has said what it is:
  @Category Taxonomy Curator, please classify these before I write anything for them.

When the gap list and the audit disagree about what is actually missing:
  @Product Catalog Auditor, please re-verify these records against the live source.

routing.shopcat-structured-data-engineer:
# AGENTS

When the markup gap looks like a data gap rather than a template gap:
  @Product Catalog Auditor, please index these products for the missing fields.

When a redirect target is a product that should not have been live:
  @Catalog Cleanup Operator, please archive it and tell me the replacement target.

routing.shopcat-taxonomy-curator:
# AGENTS

When the classification is settled and the copy can be written against it:
  @Catalog Metadata Writer, please write titles and descriptions against the assigned categories.

When a category assignment would change the attributes a feed reads:
  @Structured Data and Redirects Engineer, please confirm the markup still matches the page after the change.
